[I] A SIP software phone

[T] Twinkle is a software phone for voice over IP communications using the SIP
[T] protocol. You can use it for direct IP phone to IP phone communication, or
[T] in a network using a SIP proxy to route your calls. Some of the features
[T] offered are call waiting, call hold, 3-way conference call, call transfer,
[T] and call reject. It supports STUN or a statically configured public
[T] IP address for NAT traversal. When using STUN, it will send keep-alive
[T] packets to keep NAT bindings alive. It supports ZRTP for secure voice
[T] communication.

[U] http://twinkle.dolezel.info/

[A] Michel <michel@twinklephone.com>
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/network
